<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarhili</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1814–1892</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarhili was king of the Gcaleka Xhosa from 1835, succeeding his father Hintsa. He supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>-killing movement inspired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nongqawuse">Nongqawuse</a> in 1856 and 1857, which ruined his people, and was driven across the Mbashe river by Cape forces. Defeated in the Ninth Frontier War of 1877 and 1878, he lived in exile in Bomvanaland until his death in 1892.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarhili.jpg" alt="Sarhili" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Anon. Cape Colony. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chief_Sarili_-_Kreli_-_with_councillors.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
